Example: buying a fund with selected cash is an internal exchange.
The portfolio receives 100 USD of salary on 2023-01-01 and keeps it until
2023-07-01, when it buys one FUND unit for 100 USD. Both cash and FUND are
selected, so the -100 USD cash movement and +100 USD fund acquisition cancel.
Only the original salary inflow contributes to the portfolio over the report year.
The unit closes at 100 USD on purchase day and 120 USD on 2024-01-01.
Opening value is 0, net contributions are 100, and ending value is 120 USD.
Profit/loss is 120 - 0 - 100 = 20 USD. Time-weighted return is 20%, and the
100 USD received exactly 365 days before the end gives a 20% money-weighted
return as well.

========== CLI ==========

ledlight investment-performance --accounts '^Assets:' --commodities USD --commodities FUND --from 2023-01-01 --to 2024-01-01 --format text

========== FILE ==========

commodity USD
  default
  format 1,000.00 USD
commodity FUND
  format 1,000 FUND
account Assets:Cash
account Assets:Fund
account Income:Salary
P 2023-07-01 FUND 100 USD
P 2024-01-01 FUND 120 USD

2023-01-01 Salary
  Assets:Cash  100 USD
  Income:Salary  -100 USD

2023-07-01 Purchase
  Assets:Fund  1 FUND {100 USD}
  Assets:Cash  -100 USD

========== OUTPUT ==========

Investment performance from 2023-01-01 to 2024-01-01
Instruments: 2
Opening value: 0.00 USD
Net contributions: 100.00 USD
Ending value: 120.00 USD
Profit/loss: 20.00 USD
Time-weighted return: 20.00 %
Money-weighted return (total): 20.00 %
Money-weighted return (annualized): 20.00 %

========== WARNINGS ==========
